# Oracle samples, round r15 (2026-11-03).
# Format: BRANCH | ID | WHAT IT PROBES -> OUTPUT THAT CONFIRMS IT | SCRIPT
# SCRIPT is one batch file; "\n" separates its lines (written with CRLF). Run as a .bat file.
X | T1 | trailing ^^ after IF command -> R=0 if next line joined, R=1 if not | @echo off\nset R=0\nif 1==1 echo a ^^\nset R=1\nset R
X | T2 | REM ending in caret -> R=0 if next line swallowed | @echo off\nset R=0\nrem x ^\nset R=1\nset R
X | T3 | double-colon label ending in caret -> R=0 if next line swallowed | @echo off\nset R=0\n:: x ^\nset R=1\nset R
X | T4 | quoted redirect glued to exit /b -> no FELL and no R if exit ran | @echo off\n>"%TEMP%\a b.txt"exit /b\necho FELL\nset R=1\nset R
X | T5 | close paren line outside block with & exit /b -> FELL if line ignored | @echo off\nset x=(\n) & exit /b\necho FELL\nset R=1\nset R
X | T6 | close paren line outside block with & set -> R=1 if rest of line ran | @echo off\n) & set R=1\nset R
